<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dionysius of Phocaea</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">early 5th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dionysius of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phocaea">Phocaea</a> was a Greek naval commander during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ionian-revolt">Ionian Revolt</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a>. Before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-lade">Battle of Lade</a> in 494 BCE the Ionian fleet put him in charge of its training, though <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a> says the crews soon tired of his hard drill. After the defeat at Lade he sailed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phoenicia">Phoenicia</a>, captured merchant ships and then became a pirate off <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>, attacking Carthaginian and Etruscan shipping.</p></div>
